[Event "London System"]
[Orientation "white"]
[Pitch "One setup against almost everything: d4, Bf4, e3, c3 and a solid, easy middle game."]

1. d4 { Take the centre with the queen's pawn. } 1... d5
( 1... Nf6 2. Bf4 { The London bishop comes out before e3 shuts it in. } 2... g6
3. e3 { Support d4 and open a path for the other bishop. } 3... Bg7
4. Nf3 { Develop and control e5. } 4... O-O
5. Be2 { A safe square; against ...g6 the bishop has little to do on d3. } 5... d6
6. h3 { Give the bishop on f4 a retreat on h2 if ...Nh5 or ...e5 comes. } )
2. Bf4 { The London bishop comes out before e3 shuts it in. } 2... Nf6
( 2... c5 3. e3 { Keep d4 protected; the centre holds. } 3... Nc6
4. c3 { The London pyramid: d4 is now rock solid. } 4... Nf6
5. Nd2 { This knight goes to d2 so the queen keeps an eye on b3 and c2. } 5... e6
6. Ngf3 { Develop and control e5. } 6... Bd6 )
3. e3 { Support d4 and open a path for the other bishop. } 3... e6
4. Nf3 { Develop and control e5. } 4... c5
5. c3 { The London pyramid: d4 is now rock solid. } 5... Nc6
6. Nbd2 { This knight goes to d2 so the queen keeps an eye on b3 and c2. } 6... Bd6
7. Bg3 { Keep the bishop: if Black takes on g3, the h-file opens for you. } 7... O-O
